oss the System Lifetime\",\n      \"what\": \"Recital 71 demands that technical documentation stay current across the full lifetime of a high-risk system, covering algorithms, training data, risk-management outputs, and known limitations. We will build a versioned, living-documentation repository tied to each deployed model.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will assign a documentation steward per project, automate change-trigger alerts so that any model update or retraining event flags the corresponding document for review, and conduct quarterly internal audits verifying completeness against Article 12 scope.\",\n      \"why\": \"A defensible, always-current documentation trail is our strongest evidence of compliance in any regulator inquiry and protects market reputation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Post-Market Monitoring Dashboard for Deployed Systems\",\n      \"what\": \"Article 12 ties logging directly to post-market monitoring under Article 72, so we will build an internal observability dashboard that ingests production logs from all deployed high-risk systems and surfaces risk indicators in near real time.\",\n      \"how\": \"Our data-engineering team will develop a centralised log-ingestion pipeline with configurable alert thresholds mapped to Article 79(1) risk categories, and I will define the reporting cadence required for our post-market monitoring obligations.\",\n      \"why\": \"Operationalising this internally means we detect and document incidents before a regulator asks us to, converting a compliance burden into an early-warning asset that strengthens client trust.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
