ty (rather than a \"patchwork\" fix) signals professional maturity to regulators and clients.\n    *   *Resource Efficiency (Internal):* Reusing existing tooling (Prometheus/Loki) reduces procurement overhead and implementation friction.\n\n    *   The proposal directly addresses the legal requirements of Article 12.\n    *   It solves a current organizational vulnerability (fragmentation).\n    *   It provides a \"single audit point,\" which is exactly what a Compliance Officer wants to see for efficiency and risk mitigation.\n    *   The use of hashes for input data (instead of raw data) may be an intelligent move for privacy/GDPR compliance while still satisfying the traceability requirement of Art 12(3)(c), provided the hash is sufficient to identify the match.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal directly operationalizes Article 12 requirements through a standardized framework, eliminating fragmented evidence and creating a centralized audit trail that significantly reduces regulatory risk. Leveraging existing infrastructure ensures rapid deployment without introducing new vendor dependencies.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 95 (Very high because it solves both the technical requirement and the organizational liability of fragmentation).",
