ce monitoring so developers don't have to manually dig through logs during an audit or incident. But I dislike \"cells\" or \"committees\" if they create bureaucratic friction. However, the proposal describes a *monitoring* cell that receives alerts, not a *governance* board that blocks deployments. It transforms a regulatory requirement into a standard Ops/SRE-style monitoring workflow.\n\n    *   The proposal is essentially an operationalization of the logs required by Article 12.\n    *   From a technical viability standpoint, it's very feasible (it's basically just Site Reliability Engineering for compliance).\n    *   It protects the devs from \"regulatory surprise\" (which is a huge win for stability and quality).\n\n    *   Rationale: The proposal leverages existing telemetry/logging patterns to automate compliance monitoring, which reduces the manual burden on R&D teams during audits. It is technically straightforward and transforms a static requirement into an operational safeguard.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (High promise because it's practical and protects the engineering team, though slightly docked because \"cells\" can sometimes become bureaucratic).",
