 scientific perspective? No, because \"logging\" is essential for empirical science. If we don't log, we aren't doing reproducible research.\n\n    *   *Rationale:* Ensuring comprehensive logging during the prototyping phase provides the necessary telemetry for rigorous post-hoc analysis and failure mode identification, which are critical for maintaining scientific integrity in high-risk AI development. This systematic approach reduces technical debt and prevents retrospective data gaps that would otherwise hinder the intellectual merit of our research evaluations.\n    *   *Decision:* approve.\n    *   *Promise:* 85 (High utility because it bridges the gap between compliance and scientific rigor).",
