ary for logging that ensures compliance across all high-risk projects, it's a huge win for productivity.\n    *   Storing intermediate activations (as mentioned in the proposal) is a known technical nightmare in ML deployment (memory blowup). A compression scheme for auditability is highly viable and necessary for real-world performance.\n    *   The \"formal taxonomy\" prevents haphazard logging across different teams, making post-market monitoring much easier to implement technically.\n\n    *   *Rationale:* This proposal addresses a critical technical bottleneck—the tension between detailed forensic logging and system performance—by creating reusable standards and compression methods that benefit all high-risk project teams.\n    *   *Decision:* approve.\n    *   *Promise:* 85 (High value because it's both a compliance necessity and a technical optimization, though the \"research\" aspect is slightly slower than a pure engineering fix).",
