ng.\" We are turning a regulatory requirement into an academic exercise.\n    *   The cost of implementing a framework where researchers must write protocols for every compliance log trigger is high relative to the utility (which is primarily academic prestige/publication, not necessarily better risk mitigation than standard monitoring).\n\n    *   Rationale: While intellectually stimulating, this transforms a straightforward regulatory requirement into an expensive scientific overhead that demands significant engineering resources for bespoke pipeline configurations. It prioritizes publication potential over operational efficiency and resource conservation.\n    *   Decision: Reject.\n    *   Promise: 30 (It's clever, but too costly/over-engineered for the goal of compliance).",
