enefit to the research function.\n    *   While it has no intrinsic intellectual merit, its *instrumental* value for scientific impact (by freeing up researcher time and ensuring compliance doesn't stifle experimentation) is high.\n\n    *   Rationale: By abstracting regulatory record-keeping into shared infrastructure, researchers can maintain focus on core scientific innovation and prototyping velocity rather than repetitive compliance engineering. This prevents the \"regulatory tax\" from slowing down exploration of the knowledge frontier across multiple projects.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (High value because it removes a significant friction point for R&D, though it's not an \"AI discovery\" itself).",
