sk of late-stage project failure or illegal deployment.\n    *   This is a prudent administrative control that mitigates operational and legal risk.\n\n    *   Rationale: Integrating compliance requirements into the initial resource planning phase prevents costly retrofitting and ensures that high-risk systems are developed with Article 12 capabilities as a core requirement rather than an afterthought. This approach directly mitigates the risk of non-compliance at the point of deployment, safeguarding institutional survival and reputation.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: High (90+), because it's a low-cost/high-impact organizational change that ensures technical requirements are actually met.",
