grity of the development process.\n    *   It doesn't seem to stifle innovation; rather, it provides a safety net so researchers don't spend weeks on a prototype only to find out later that none of the required telemetry was captured, making it impossible to validate according to regulatory standards (which would waste research resources).\n\n    *   Rationale: Automating the verification of traceability requirements ensures that experimental results remain reproducible and compliant without adding manual overhead to the research cycle. This protects the intellectual merit of the work by preventing the loss of critical operational telemetry during rapid prototyping.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (around 85-90), because it's a practical engineering solution that supports scientific rigor without impeding the speed of exploration.",
