s of Article 12(1), 12(2), and 12(3) by creating a technical enforcement mechanism.\n    *   It mitigates the risk of human error (forgetting to implement logging) by integrating it into the pipeline.\n    *   It protects institutional survival by ensuring EU market access is not jeopardized by basic compliance failures.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal operationalizes Article 12 by embedding mandatory, standardized logging into the development lifecycle, effectively eliminating the risk of deploying non-compliant high-risk systems. It directly safeguards institutional survival and market access by preventing costly retroactive fixes and regulatory penalties.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 95 (extremely strong, though perhaps a small deduction because \"configurable schemas\" still require human oversight to ensure the *correct* events are logged for specific use cases).",
