d prototyping. However, the proposal specifically mentions keeping \"iteration speed intact\" by providing specific diagnostics and shifting verification left.\n\n    *   The proposal ensures that any system moving toward integration is actually traceable. This supports scientific rigor. It doesn't inherently block research; it just mandates a standard for output data (logs).\n    *   From the perspective of \"intellectual merit,\" having robust, machine-verifiable logs is essential for debugging complex emergent behaviors in AI systems—a key part of pushing the knowledge frontier.\n\n    *   Rationale: This automation ensures that empirical traceability is baked into the development process, supporting scientific rigor and reproducibility without burdening researchers with manual compliance audits. It converts regulatory requirements into a technical standard that protects the integrity of research data throughout the system's lifetime.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (High utility for maintaining standards, though it is more engineering-focused than purely theoretical).",
