 we are acting in good faith and have institutional control.\n    *   *Alignment with Article 12:* While the proposal isn't about *how* to log (the technical implementation), it is the essential *prerequisite* for knowing *where* to implement logging. You cannot satisfy Article 12 without first identifying which systems are \"high-risk\" per Annex III.\n\n    *   Rationale: This provides the necessary governance framework to identify high-risk systems early, ensuring that the technical requirements of Article 12 are integrated into the development lifecycle rather than added as a costly afterthought. It directly mitigates legal and financial risks associated with non-compliance and late-stage redesigns.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 95 (High confidence because triage is the foundation of any compliance regime).",
